  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact Cluster: Onion Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the project is to support Bangladesh in developing new and improved onion value chains by introducing innovative Dutch solutions and expertise for onion production and storage, thereby contributing to local private sector development, increased income of farmers and entrepreneurs in the onion sector and reduced onion imports.The project interventions address two related problems in the onion supply chain in Bangladesh:1.	Lack of improved onion seed, and inadequate postharvest and storage practices;2.	Lack of knowledge and skills to adopt improved solutions and technologies.Onion varieties to be introduced by the project will be tested to deliver higher yields and enable longer shelf life while storage solutions will be designed to extend the shelf life of both local and improved onion varieties. As a result, the project will contribute to increasing the local production and the availability of onion on the Bangladeshi market.</narrative>
  </description>
